  {
    "key": "trace",
    "url": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22760894",
    "status": 200,
    "sha256": "2e608f0dbf6f7dfa2a8dc0bb7fb25a0be609b08a2a0ac9ddfb0df0b0304239a1",
    "data": {
      "created": "2026-09-15T12:22:19.670883+00:00",
      "modified": "2026-09-15T12:22:20.044379+00:00",
      "id": 22760894,
      "conceptrecid": "20408339",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22760894",
      "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20408339",
      "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22760894",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "Trace-IN625: a source aware literature derived dataset of tensile properties and microstructure for additively manufactured IN625",
        "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22760894",
        "publication_date": "2026-09-15",
        "description": "<p>Trace-IN625 is a source-aware, literature-derived dataset of tensile properties and supporting microstructure information for additively manufactured IN625. It organizes published measurements into individually retrievable material-condition records, preserving source references, processing and heat-treatment information, measurement definitions and test context where available. The resource supports literature-based comparison of tensile properties and inspection of the published evidence associated with reported material states.</p>\n<p>The literature index contains <strong>305 publications</strong>, of which <strong>72 contribute the 149 retained tensile-property records</strong>. These records contain <strong>391 populated property values</strong>: 114 yield-strength values, 139 ultimate-tensile-strength values and 138 elongation values. The tensile layer distinguishes <strong>120 IN625 records</strong> from <strong>29 records concerning IN625-containing composite, graded or joined materials</strong>, enabling users to select the relevant material population before analysis.</p>\n<p>The release comprises six core tables in UTF-8 CSV format:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>papers.csv &mdash; 305 records:</strong> bibliographic information and identifiers for the indexed source publications.</li>\n<li><strong>specimens.csv &mdash; 482 records:</strong> specimen labels, material states or source conditions, with associated processing and post-treatment information. These entries do not represent 482 independent experimental replicates.</li>\n<li><strong>tensile_properties.csv &mdash; 149 records:</strong> reported tensile properties, measurement definitions, test conditions, source locators and available uncertainty information.</li>\n<li><strong>microstructure_records.csv &mdash; 2,206 records:</strong> microstructure descriptions and source-text or figure evidence. This layer is predominantly descriptive and indexed evidence, rather than a collection of quantitative microstructural measurements.</li>\n<li><strong>figure_index.csv &mdash; 2,263 records:</strong> indexed source figures or graphical objects, including provenance and public-crop availability.</li>\n<li><strong>image_crops_manifest.csv &mdash; 280 records:</strong> metadata for the <strong>280 released PNG crops</strong>, including identifiers, file paths, checksums, dimensions, source attribution and licence information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The package also includes a data dictionary, controlled vocabularies, source-review records, validation outputs, plotting data, retrieval examples and executable release-checking scripts. Linked identifiers connect publications, material conditions, tensile records and figure evidence. Source checking combines AI-assisted comparison with the publications and author review; accompanying software checks assess relational consistency and deposited-file integrity.</p>\n<p>Reuse should account for material scope, processing state, measurement definition, temperature and loading direction. Missing values and unspecified uncertainties must not be interpreted as zero. Qualitative room-temperature descriptions are retained separately from numerical temperatures, and explicitly identified true-strain values remain distinguishable from other elongation quantities.</p>\n<p>The image collection provides contextual evidence from published figures. It does not contain instrument-native characterization data or raw EBSD orientation maps, and shared publication identifiers do not establish specimen-level correspondence between micrographs and tensile measurements.</p>\n<p>Structured metadata are released under <strong>CC BY 4.0</strong>. Third-party image crops retain their recorded source-specific licences; attribution and modification details are provided in <strong>image_crops_manifest.csv</strong> and <strong>LICENSING.md</strong>. Full source PDFs are not included.</p>",
